      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Most of the issues around children and pain have been identified and yet children's pain continues to be poorly managed. This review aims to take a fresh look at this topic through the use of family nursing theory and children's policy and rights perspectives. Family nursing and children's policy have a valuable contribution to make to assessment issues; nurse education needs to combine family-centred care concepts and children's rights in the teaching of pain management."},
